  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sanitation for All</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to provide an innovative solution to an unaddressed need within humanitarian responses: the of a lack of suitable access to sanitation for people with incontinence and very young children. These individuals are either not provided with a solution to their sanitary needs, or provided with disposable solutions, thereby being both expensive, difficult to safely dispose of within humanitarian contexts, and not environmentally friendly. This project seeks to meet the needs by proposing a solution that is sustainable and better for the environment, reduces the burden on caregivers, and promotes the local economy through local production through a financially sustainable model.</narrative>
  </description>
